#. module: muk_ai_skills
#: model:muk_ai.skill,body:muk_ai_skills.demo_skill_draft_followup
msgid ""
"# Draft Follow-up\n"
"\n"
"Draft a tactful follow-up message to a partner. Do not send anything;\n"
"return the draft for the user to review:\n"
"\n"
"1. Resolve the target partner (model `res.partner` + id or pinned\n"
"   record). If missing, `ask_user` once.\n"
"2. Use `search_read` on `mail.message` with domain\n"
"   `[('model','=','res.partner'),('res_id','=',<id>),\n"
"   ('message_type','in',['comment','email'])]`, order\n"
"   `date desc`, limit 3, fields `date,subject,body,author_id`.\n"
"   This grounds the follow-up in real prior context.\n"
"3. Compose a draft:\n"
"   - Tone: warm, professional, plain prose.\n"
"   - Length cap: 90 words.\n"
"   - Reference the most recent prior interaction concretely (date\n"
"     + topic). If there is none, open with a soft re-introduction.\n"
"   - End with a single, low-friction next step (a question or a\n"
"     proposed slot), not a hard ask.\n"
"4. Output the draft as a plain message, no preamble. After the draft,\n"
"   one short line listing the prior messages you used. Stop.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: muk_ai_skills
#: model:muk_ai.skill,body:muk_ai_skills.demo_skill_explain_record
msgid ""
"# Explain a Record\n"
"\n"
"Given a model + id (or the currently pinned record from the view\n"
"context), produce a short briefing the user can read in 30 seconds:\n"
"\n"
"1. If model + id is missing, use the pinned record from `<ui_ctx>`.\n"
"   If still missing, call `ask_user` for the record reference.\n"
"2. Use `read_records` to fetch the record. Pass an explicit `fields`\n"
"   list scoped to the user-meaningful fields (skip technical or\n"
"   internal fields unless asked).\n"
"3. Output:\n"
"   - Header line: `Display Name (model,id)`\n"
"   - Up to 8 key/value bullets (label · value).\n"
"   - One-line state/lifecycle note (\"draft\", \"in progress\",\n"
"     \"blocked by X\").\n"
"   - Top 3 most recent log notes from `mail.message` (skip\n"
"     auto/system) with author and date.\n"
"4. Stop. Do not propose actions unless asked.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: muk_ai_skills
#: model:muk_ai.skill,body:muk_ai_skills.demo_skill_partner_brief
msgid ""
"# Partner Brief\n"
"\n"
"Produce a short business briefing the user can read in 30 seconds for\n"
"a single partner record:\n"
"\n"
"1. Resolve the target partner: model `res.partner` + id (or pinned\n"
"   record from `<ui_ctx>`). If still missing, call `ask_user` once.\n"
"2. Use `read_records` to fetch the partner. Limit `fields` to the\n"
"   user-meaningful set: `name`, `is_company`, `email`, `phone`,\n"
"   `country_id`, `city`, `industry_id`, `customer_rank`,\n"
"   `supplier_rank`, `category_id`, `user_id`, `parent_id`.\n"
"3. Use `search_read` on `mail.message` with domain\n"
"   `[('model','=','res.partner'),('res_id','=',<id>),\n"
"   ('message_type','in',['comment','email'])]`, order\n"
"   `date desc`, limit 5, fields `author_id,date,subject,body`.\n"
"4. Output:\n"
"   - Header: `Display Name (res.partner,<id>) — Company / Contact`\n"
"   - 5-7 key/value bullets (label · value), skipping empties.\n"
"   - \"Recent activity\" line listing the 3 most recent log dates +\n"
"     short subject.\n"
"   - One-line relationship summary: customer / supplier / both /\n"
"     prospect, plus the salesperson if set.\n"
"5. Stop. Do not propose actions unless asked.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: muk_ai_skills
#: model:muk_ai.skill,body:muk_ai_skills.demo_skill_safe_archive
msgid ""
"# Safe Archive\n"
"\n"
"Archive records (`active = False`) only after explicit user\n"
"confirmation, with a structured preview:\n"
"\n"
"1. Resolve the target set: model + domain (or model + ids). If\n"
"   ambiguous, call `ask_user` once.\n"
"2. Use `search_count` to count the target set. If `> 50`, summarise\n"
"   that count and ask the user to confirm before listing.\n"
"3. Use `search_read` (limit 25) to fetch `id`, `display_name`, and\n"
"   any obviously linked counts (e.g. `sale_order_count`,\n"
"   `invoice_ids`). Show in a small table.\n"
"4. Call `ask_user` with `resolution='yesno'` and a structured\n"
"   `preview` of kind `update`, listing the targets and the\n"
"   `active: True → False` change. Stop.\n"
"5. On the user's \"yes\" answer (the next turn), call\n"
"   `update_records` to archive in one batch. Reply with one line:\n"
"   N records archived.\n"
msgstr ""

